          "steps": [
            {
              "short": "Proxy",
              "chapter": "problem",
              "title": "Every photo goes through the API",
              "body": [
                "Today the app sends the full photo — about <b>8 MB</b> — to the Upload API, which streams it on to object storage.",
                "Each upload holds an API worker for the whole transfer. On a slow phone network that's 10+ seconds, so a busy evening fills every worker and even small requests start timing out."
              ],
              "callout": {
                "kind": "warn",
                "text": "When the API carries bytes it doesn't need to look at, its capacity is set by your users' network speed, not by your code."
              },
              "metrics": {
                "p99": 9200,
                "ok": 91,
                "cpu": 94,
                "lag": "—"
              },
              "scene": {
                "entities": {
                  "users": true,
                  "api": {
                    "heat": 0.85,
                    "cpu": 0.94,
                    "tags": [
                      {
                        "text": "streaming 8 MB bodies",
                        "tone": "red",
                        "icon": "hourglass"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  "store": true
                },
                "links": {
                  "ua": {
                    "label": "POST /photos (8 MB)",
                    "labelTone": "red",
                    "fail": 0.15
                  },
                  "as": true
                },
                "flows": [
                  {
                    "route": [
                      "ua",
                      "as"
                    ],
                    "kind": "heavy",
                    "rate": 1.6,
                    "bounce": true
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "short": "Presign",
              "chapter": "solution",
              "title": "Hand out a presigned URL instead",
              "body": [
                "The app now asks the API for permission first. The API checks the user and returns a <span class=\"term\">presigned URL</span>: a storage address that accepts one upload, for one key, for five minutes.",
                "The bytes then go <b>straight to storage</b>. The API only handles tiny JSON requests."
              ],
              "callout": {
                "kind": "tip",
                "text": "Sign only what you need: fixed key, content-type and a max size. A leaked URL then can't be used to upload anything else."
              },
              "changes": [
                "+ POST /uploads returns a signed URL",
                "~ Bytes go app → storage directly",
                "~ API CPU 94% → 22%"
              ],
              "metrics": {
                "p99": 2600,
                "ok": 98,
                "cpu": 22,
                "lag": "—"
              },
              "scene": {
                "entities": {
                  "users": true,
                  "api": {
                    "cpu": 0.22
                  },
                  "store": true
                },
                "links": {
                  "ua": {
                    "label": "POST /uploads"
                  },
                  "us": true
                },
                "flows": [
                  {
                    "route": [
                      "ua"
                    ],
                    "rate": 1.4,
                    "bounce": true
                  },
                  {
                    "route": [
                      "us"
                    ],
                    "kind": "heavy",
                    "rate": 1.4,
                    "bounce": true
                  }
                ],
                "card": {
                  "title": "The new upload handshake",
                  "icon": "key",
                  "lines": [
                    "1  POST /uploads        → { url, key, expires: 5 min }",
                    "2  PUT  <signed url>    → 200  (8 MB, app → storage)",
                    "3  POST /uploads/:key/complete",
                    "# the API never touches the photo bytes"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "short": "Metadata",
              "chapter": "technique",
              "title": "Record the upload before it happens",
              "body": [
                "When it signs the URL, the API also inserts a row: <code>status = pending</code>. When the app calls <code>/complete</code>, the API checks the object really exists and flips it to <code>uploaded</code>.",
                "Now every photo has a single source of truth, even if the app crashes halfway."
              ],
              "callout": {
                "kind": "insight",
                "text": "Never trust the client's “done” — verify the object (size, type) in storage before marking it uploaded."
              },
              "changes": [
                "+ photos table (pending → uploaded)",
                "+ /complete verifies the object"
              ],
              "metrics": {
                "p99": 2600,
                "ok": 99,
                "cpu": 24,
                "lag": "—"
              },
              "scene": {
                "entities": {
                  "users": true,
                  "api": {
                    "cpu": 0.24
                  },
                  "store": true,
                  "db": {
                    "tags": [
                      {
                        "text": "status: pending → uploaded",
                        "tone": "amber",
                        "icon": "clock"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "links": {
                  "ua": {
                    "label": "POST /uploads"
                  },
                  "us": true,
                  "ad": {
                    "label": "INSERT · UPDATE"
                  }
                },
                "flows": [
                  {
                    "route": [
                      "ua",
                      "ad"
                    ],
                    "rate": 1.2,
                    "bounce": true
                  },
                  {
                    "route": [
                      "us"
                    ],
                    "kind": "heavy",
                    "rate": 1.2,
                    "bounce": true
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "short": "Thumbnails",
              "chapter": "technique",
              "title": "Make thumbnails in the background",
              "body": [
                "The feed needs small versions of every photo. Instead of resizing during the upload, storage emits an <span class=\"term\">object-created event</span> into a queue.",
                "A thumbnail worker pulls jobs, writes 3 sizes back to storage and marks the photo <code>ready</code>. Uploads finish as soon as the bytes land."
              ],
              "callout": {
                "kind": "tip",
                "text": "The queue absorbs bursts: 10,000 uploads at 9 pm just means a longer queue for a minute, not a slower upload."
              },
              "changes": [
                "+ Event → resize queue",
                "+ Thumbnail worker (3 sizes)",
                "~ Upload p99 2.6 s → 1.4 s"
              ],
              "metrics": {
                "p99": 1400,
                "ok": 99,
                "cpu": 24,
                "lag": {
                  "value": "~4 s",
                  "level": "good"
                }
              },
              "scene": {
                "entities": {
                  "users": true,
                  "api": {
                    "cpu": 0.24
                  },
                  "store": true,
                  "db": true,
                  "queue": true,
                  "worker": {
                    "cpu": 0.45
                  }
                },
                "links": {
                  "ua": true,
                  "us": true,
                  "ad": true,
                  "sq": true,
                  "qw": true,
                  "ws": true
                },
                "flows": [
