            {
              "short": "CDN",
              "chapter": "technique",
              "title": "Serve photos from a CDN",
              "body": [
                "Viewing is 50× more common than uploading. Photos are now served by a <span class=\"term\">CDN</span> with long cache headers — the key includes a content hash, so a URL never changes meaning.",
                "Most views never reach storage; only cache misses do."
              ],
              "callout": {
                "kind": "tip",
                "text": "Immutable, hashed URLs let you cache for a year and still “update” a photo — by giving it a new URL."
              },
              "changes": [
                "+ CDN in front of storage",
                "~ 96% of views are cache hits"
              ],
